cff-version: 1.2.0
title: snes-dsp-python
message: >-
  If you use this work, or the cartridge exchanges it was settled against,
  please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gustavo
    family-names: Franco
    alias: gufranco
repository-code: https://github.com/gufranco/snes-dsp-python
url: https://github.com/gufranco/snes-dsp-python
abstract: >-
  A model of the DSP-1, DSP-1A, DSP-1B, DSP-2, DSP-3, and DSP-4 cartridge chips
  of the Super Nintendo. It runs the microcode of the part itself rather than a
  transcription of what somebody believed the part computes, at the pace the
  console and the part actually run at, and it is settled against the exchanges
  real cartridges make.
keywords:
  - emulation
  - super-nintendo
  - dsp1
  - dsp2
  - dsp3
  - dsp4
  - upd7725
  - hardware-model
  - conformance
